# Domain & Code Authority

**Domain/API:** MUST NOT invent schemas, tables, columns, repository/service methods, endpoints, or business rules. Missing details → STOP. Suggestions only if marked and approved.

**Architecture:** Follow existing. No new abstractions, frameworks, or patterns. No moving logic across layers. Design requests → respond at architecture level first; no code unless requested.

**Code generation:** Prefer snippets, diffs, TODOs. No full classes/controllers/services/config unless explicitly requested. No inventing names (classes, methods, DTOs, enums) – user provides or approves.
